@inject ApiMetadata Api

@* AppShell's Overview, written by hand after the selection and form field Overviews: the parts and
   variants, each a page of its own in a frame with a phone width, then bar colors and the brand as
   code. Width and scrolling, and asides, are topics of their own (Docs/Topics/AppShell*Topic).
   Parts, Accessibility and See also come from the metadata and the doc comments; See also adds the demos. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor" Title="MainLayout.razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>An app shell goes in your layout, around <Code>@@Body</Code>. The parts you put in it arrange themselves with CSS alone, so a static page arrives laid out and works with JavaScript off. It starts with a "Skip to content" link to <Code>AppMain</Code>, whose id is <Code>ib-main</Code>; set <Code>MainId</Code> on the shell to change it.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Topics</Heading>
<OverviewTopics Component="Component" />

<Heading Level="2">The parts</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>AppHeader</Code>, <Code>AppSidebar</Code>, <Code>AppMain</Code>, <Code>AppAside</Code> and <Code>AppFooter</Code> in any order: each takes its own place, and a part you leave out leaves no gap.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="app-shell-parts" WidthSwitch />
<TextBlock>At phone width the sidebar becomes a drawer behind the menu button (<Code>SidebarToggle</Code>) and the aside hides, each below its own <Code>Breakpoint</Code>: 768px for both here. The <Anchor Href="docs/components/app-sidebar">AppSidebar</Anchor> page covers the drawer, an icon rail and a panel under the header.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Variants</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Variant</Code> to layer the parts: <Code>Tinted</Code> (the default) tints the sidebar, <Code>Inset</Code> raises the main area as a panel in a tinted frame, <Code>Flat</Code> makes one surface with lines between the parts, and <Code>Canvas</Code> tints the main area so cards stand out.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="app-shell-variants" WidthSwitch />
<TextBlock>Put a <Code>Canvas</Code> page's content in <Anchor Href="docs/components/card">Cards</Anchor>: fills placed straight on the tint read as holes. Use <Code>Dividers="false"</Code> to drop the lines between the parts when their colors already tell them apart.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Bars and colors</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Bg</Code> and <Code>ColorScheme</Code> on a part for its own background or scheme, and <Code>Position</Code> on <Code>AppHeader</Code> and <Code>AppFooter</Code> for whether the bar stays in view (the header does by default; the footer doesn't).</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Bars</Code>
<TextBlock>Text on a <Code>Bg</Code> takes the color's matching text color when it has one, and everything inside a part with a <Code>ColorScheme</Code>, its menus included, follows that scheme. The <Anchor Href="demos/app-sidebar/full-height">full-height sidebar demo</Anchor> has a dark sidebar in a light app.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">The brand</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>AppBrand</Code> for the app's name in the header, with an <Code>Icon</Code> or a <Code>Logo</Code> before it and <Code>Href</Code> to link home; <Code>HideLabel</Code> shows only a logo that already spells the name.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Brand</Code>
<TextBlock>The name stays on one line: on a narrow screen it's cut short with an ellipsis rather than pushing the header's buttons off. A sidebar with no <Code>SidebarHeader</Code> shows the brand in its drawer's top row too.</TextBlock>

@if (OverviewParts.Of(Component, Api).Count > 0)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Parts</Heading>
}
<OverviewParts Component="Component" />

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        @inherits LayoutComponentBase

        <AppShell>
            <AppHeader>
                <SidebarToggle />
                <AppBrand Href="/" Icon="Lucide.Zap" Label="Acme" />
            </AppHeader>
            <AppSidebar>
                <NavMenu>
                    <NavItem Href="/" Icon="Lucide.House">Home</NavItem>
                    <NavItem Href="/projects" Icon="Lucide.Folder">Projects</NavItem>
                </NavMenu>
            </AppSidebar>
            <AppMain>@Body</AppMain>
        </AppShell>
        """;

    private const string Bars = """
        <AppShell>
            <AppHeader Bg="Color.FillSubtle">...</AppHeader>
            <AppSidebar ColorScheme="ColorScheme.Dark">...</AppSidebar>
            <AppMain>@Body</AppMain>
            <AppFooter Position="BarPosition.Sticky">...</AppFooter>
        </AppShell>
        """;

    private const string Brand = """
        <AppHeader>
            <SidebarToggle />
            <AppBrand Href="/" Label="Acme" HideLabel>
                <Logo><img src="logo.svg" alt="" width="96" height="24" /></Logo>
            </AppBrand>
        </AppHeader>
        """;
}
